&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 11&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50063349</guid><pubDate>Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:34:23 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Vibecheck – merge gate that checks you understand your AI-written code</title><link>https://github.com/bhurghundii/vibecheck.dev</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Good evening folks, I built Github merge gate which that checks whether developers understand their own code when they create a PR.&lt;p&gt;I kept getting sent PRs to review where it was obvious the author had pasted the ticket into an LLM and called it a day.&lt;p&gt;It's self-hosted (so you can use it in your enterprise environments or privately)&lt;p&gt;It is BYOK (Anthropic) obviously.&lt;p&gt;I have two demos in the pull requests here: &lt;a href="https://github.com/bhurghundii/vibecheck.dev/pulls" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://github.com/bhurghundii/vibecheck.dev/pulls&lt;/a&gt; - you can see what Vibecheck does (it blocks a PR for clearly showing no attempt vs a PR which gets it right)&lt;p&gt;I would love feedback, especially from anyone dealing with a similar problem. I do use it for my own projects a lot so expect improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
